  "slug": "yuca-frita",
  "name": "Yuca Frita",
  "recipe_type": "appetizer",
  "brief_description": "This is a tasty Latin side dish, that I always enjoy making. It's a great alternative to french fries or potatoes. This is also great if your looking for a real, ethnic appetizer or tapa!",
  "cuisine": "Latin American Latin",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Heat the oil in a large heavy skillet over medium-high heat. Place the yuca fries in the hot oil and fry until golden brown, about 20 minutes. Turn occasionally to brown them evenly. Remove from the skillet with a slotted spoon or spatula and season with salt. Squeeze lime juice over them if you like and serve immediately."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 2,
